{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Public Safety and Homeland Security to make an investigation and study of a certain current Senate document relative to emergency response.\r\n\r\n","BillNumber":"S2774","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J22","Name":"Joint Committee on Public Safety and Homeland Security","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22","ResponseDate":"2024-05-07T09:50:45.237"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2774/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"The committee on Public Safety and Homeland Security, to whom was referred the petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1581) of Rebecca L. Rausch for legislation to band the use of tear gas against civilians, report the accompanying Order (Senate, No. 2774).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Public Safety and Homeland Security be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of a certain current Senate document numbered 1581 relative to emergency response.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}